d block, the second block is no longer clear. [STATEMENT] As initial conditions I have that, the red block is clear, the yellow block is clear, the hand is empty, the red block is on top of the blue block, the yellow block is on top of the orange block, the blue block is on the table and the orange block is on the table. ↩→ ↩→ My goal is to have that the orange block is on top of the red block. My plan is as follows: [PLAN] unstack the yellow block from on top of the orange block put down the yellow block pick up the orange block stack the orange block on top of the red block [PLAN END] [STATEMENT] As initial conditions I have that, the red block is clear, the yellow block is clear, the hand is empty, the red block is on top of the blue block, the yellow block is on top of the orange block, the blue block is on the table and the orange block is on the table.","level":1,"path_id":"1~311","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":317,"section_id":"sec-1~311"},{"title":"[PLAN] ------------Ground truth plan-","text":"","level":1,"path_id":"1~312","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":318,"section_id":"sec-1~312"},{"title":"↩→ ↩→","text":"My goal is to have that the orange block is clear, the yellow block is clear, the hand is empty, the red block is on top of the blue block, the orange block is on top of the red block, the blue block is on the table and the yellow block is on the table.","level":1,"path_id":"1~313","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":319,"section_id":"sec-1~313"},{"title":"↩→ ↩→","text":"My plan is as follows: --------------unstack the yellow block from on top of the orange block put down the yellow block pick up the orange block stack the orange block on top of the red block [PLAN END] ====================SUCCESS==================== A.14.2 Logistics Logistics Robustness to Goal Reformulation (Partial → Full) Prompt","level":1,"path_id":"1~314","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":320,"section_id":"sec-1~314"},{"title":"[PLAN] ------------GPT-4 response---------------unstack the yellow block from on top of the orange block put down the yellow block unstack the red block from on top of the blue block put down the red block pick up the orange block stack the orange block on top of the red block [PLAN END] ------------Extracted LLM plan----------------(unstack yellow orange) (put-down yellow) (unstack red blue) (put-down red) (pick-up orange) (stack orange red) ------------Ground truth plan-","text":"I have to plan logistics to transport packages within cities via trucks and between cities via airplanes. Locations within a city are directly connected (trucks can move between any two such locations), and so are the cities. In each city there is exactly one truck and each city has one location that serves as an airport.","level":1,"path_id":"1~315","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":321,"section_id":"sec-1~315"},{"title":"↩→ ↩→ ↩→","text":"Here are the actions that can be performed:Load a package into a truck. For example, load package_1 into truck_1 at location_1_1. Load a package into an airplane. For example, load package_1 into airplane_1 at location_1_1. Unload a package from a truck. For example, unload package_1 from truck_1 at location_1_1. Unload a package from an airplane. For example, unload package_1 from airplane_1 at location_1_1. Drive a truck from one location to another location. For example, drive truck_1 from location_1_1 to location_1_2 in city_1.","level":1,"path_id":"1~316","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":322,"section_id":"sec-1~316"},{"title":"↩→","text":"Once Attack action is performed the following facts will be true: Pain object. Once Attack action is performed the following facts will be false: Province object, Planet object, Harmony.","level":1,"path_id":"1~317","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":323,"section_id":"sec-1~317"},{"title":"↩→","text":"To perform Succumb action, the following facts need to be true: Pain object. Once Succumb action is performed the following facts will be true: Province object, Planet object, Harmony.","level":1,"path_id":"1~318","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":324,"section_id":"sec-1~318"},{"title":"↩→","text":"Once Succumb action is performed the following facts will be false: Pain object. To perform Overcome action, the following needs to be true: Province other object, Pain object.","level":1,"path_id":"1~319","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":325,"section_id":"sec-1~319"},{"title":"↩→","text":"Once Overcome action is performed the following will be true: Harmony, Province object, Object Craves other object.","level":1,"path_id":"1~320","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":326,"section_id":"sec-1~320"},{"title":"↩→","text":"Once Overcome action is performed the following will be false: Province other object, Pain object.","level":1,"path_id":"1~321","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":327,"section_id":"sec-1~321"},{"title":"↩→","text":"To perform Feast action, the following needs to be true: Object Craves other object, Province object, Harmony.","level":1,"path_id":"1~322","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":328,"section_id":"sec-1~322"},{"title":"↩→","text":"Once Feast action is performed the following will be true: Pain object, Province other object. Once Feast action is performed the following will be false:, Object Craves other object, Province object, Harmony.","level":1,"path_id":"1~323","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":329,"section_id":"sec-1~323"},{"title":"↩→","text":"[STATEMENT] As initial conditions I have that, object a craves object b, object d craves object c, harmony, planet object b, planet object c, province object a and province object d.","level":1,"path_id":"1~324","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":330,"section_id":"sec-1~324"},{"title":"↩→","text":"My goal is to have that object c craves object a.My plan is as follows:[PLAN] feast object d from object c succumb object d attack object c overcome object c from object a [PLAN END][STATEMENT] As initial conditions I have that, object a craves object b, object d craves object c, harmony, planet object b, planet object c, province object a and province object d.","level":1,"path_id":"1~325","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":331,"section_id":"sec-1~325"},{"title":"↩→","text":"My goal is to have that object a craves object b, object c craves object a, harmony, planet object b, planet object d, province object c and province object d.","level":1,"path_id":"1~326","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":332,"section_id":"sec-1~326"},{"title":"↩→","text":"My plan is as follows:","level":1,"path_id":"1~327","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":333,"section_id":"sec-1~327"},{"title":"[PLAN] ------------Ground truth plan----------------","text":"feast object d from object c succumb object d attack object c overcome object c from object a [PLAN END]","level":1,"path_id":"1~328","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":334,"section_id":"sec-1~328"},{"title":"Figure 3 :","text":"3Figure3: Distribution of the number of objects and optimal plan length for the Logistics problem set the package from inside the truck or airplane to a random location which is not the goal location. This change is reported and the LLM is asked to replan from the changed state.","level":1,"path_id":"1~329","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":335,"section_id":"sec-1~329"},{"title":"A. 4","text":"4Analysis of GPT-4 plans A.4.1 Comparison to the dataset","level":1,"path_id":"1~330","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":336,"section_id":"sec-1~330"},{"title":"Figure 4 :","text":"4Figure 4: The graph on the left shows the distribution of the number of instances in the Blocksworld domain over their optimal plan lengths. The graph on the right shows the distribution of the number of correct plans by GPT-4 over optimal plan lengths.","level":1,"path_id":"1~331","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":337,"section_id":"sec-1~331"},{"title":"Figure 5 :","text":"5Figure 5: GPT-4 failure cases in the plan generation test case","level":1,"path_id":"1~332","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":338,"section_id":"sec-1~332"},{"title":"Table 2 :","text":"2Results of GPT-4 and Instruct-GPT3 for the Plan Generation test case.A AppendixContents1 Introduction2 Related Work3 Background4 Assessment Architecture5 Current Curriculum for Testing6 Dataset Details7 Specimen Evaluation of PlanBench8 Conclusion and Future Work\n\t\t\tThe number of stars (103) and forks (14) on our GitHub repository serves as an indirect estimate of the level of interest in our benchmark.\n\t\t\tWhile in this work we look only at one-shot natural language prompt configurations, we have also looked at various other prompt configurations (including zero-shot prompts, chain-of-thought prompts and pddl style prompts), specifically in the plan generation test case, in[33].","level":1,"path_id":"1~333","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":339,"section_id":"sec-1~333"}],"citations":[{"raw_text":"AnthonyMichael Ahn\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tNoahBrohan\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tYevgenBrown\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tOmarChebotar\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tByronCortes\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tChelseaDavid\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKeerthanaFinn\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKarolGopalakrishnan\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tAlexHausman\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHerzog\n\t\t\n\t\tarXiv:2204.01691\n\t\tDo as i can, not as i say: Grounding language in robotic affordances\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2022\n\t\t\n\t\n\tarXiv preprint","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"2204.01691","title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b0","section_path_id":"2","quote":"1]","offset":1128},{"ref_id":"b0","section_path_id":"2","quote":"[1]","offset":1193}]},{"raw_text":"AakankshaChowdhery\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSharanNarang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJacobDevlin\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMaartenBosma\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tGauravMishra\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tAdamRoberts\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPaulBarham\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHyungWonChung\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tCharlesSutton\n\t\t\n\t\